</main>\par
\par
[Coach]: Great snippet, Sampson. It clearly sets up the data injection. In this update form, you're appending <%= category_id %> right into the form's action attribute, but you also included an <input type="hidden" name="category_id" value="<%= category_id %>"> inside the form. What went into your decision to include the ID in both places, and how does your backend use them differently?\par
\par
[Sampson]: Including the ID in both the URL path and the hidden form input serves two distinct purposes on the backend, separating route matching from data processing. Placing the ID in both locations keeps the route definition decoupled from the internal data structure. If we change your URL layout later to a clean static endpoint (e.g., /category/update), the controller logic processing the form data payload inside req.body will not break, because it does not depend on data extracted from the URL path.\par
\par
[Coach]: That makes total sense. Decoupling the routing parameters (req.params) from the request payload (req.body) gives your application great flexibility if the URL structure changes later. Let's move to our third topic, Sessions and Flash Messages. Could you provide a relevant code snippet showing how you configure or utilize sessions and flash messages in your application?\par
\par
[Sampson]: \par
// configuration inside your root server.js file\par
import session from 'express-session';\par
import flash from 'connect-flash';\par
\par
app.use(session(\{\par
    secret: 'session_secret_key',\par
    resave: false,\par
    saveUninitialized: false\par
\}));\par
\par
app.use(flash());\par
\par
// Pass flash messages to all views via local variables middleware\par
app.use((req, res, next) => \{\par
    res.locals.notice = req.flash('notice');\par
    next();\par
\});\par
\par
// Utilization inside src/controllers/categories.js\par
const registerCategory = async (req, res, next) => \{\par
    const \{ category_name \} = req.body;\par
    try \{\par
        const result = await insertCategory(category_name);\par
        if (result) \{\par
            // Setting a flash message before redirecting\par
            req.flash('notice', `The $\{category_name\} category was successfully added.`);\par
            res.redirect('/categories');\par
        \} else \{\par
            req.flash('notice', 'Sorry, adding the category failed.');\par
            res.status(501).render('categories/add-category', \{\par
                title: 'Add New Category',\par
